  "text": "You are more closely related to a mushroom than a mushroom is to a tree. Everything alive runs on the same instructions. Not similar ones. The same. Same four letters of DNA. Same cell machinery. Same energy currency. Which only makes sense if life started once, and never managed it again. Run the family tree backwards far enough and every branch meets. And the tree is not the shape you picture. Fungi are on our side of it. Humans and mushrooms share roughly half of their genes. Fungi cannot photosynthesise. They have to eat, exactly like you do. Zoom out far enough and humans are one twig. Not the top of anything. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
